slml 0.2
use"layout.slml"

doc{$title"Forms"
  t.lead"Contact forms, sign-ups and surveys are written with `form` and a few field elements. Every field must have a visible label."
  section{$id"example" $title"A contact form"
    demo{$code"form(to: \"https://formspree.io/f/your-id\", method: post, gap: 14) {\n  input(name: \"name\", label: \"Your name\", required: true)\n  input(name: \"email\", label: \"E-mail\", kind: email,\n        placeholder: \"you@example.com\", required: true)\n  select(name: \"topic\", label: \"Topic\") {\n    option \"Question\"\n    option \"Feedback\"\n  }\n  textarea(name: \"message\", label: \"Message\", rows: 4)\n  checkbox(name: \"newsletter\", label: \"Send me news\")\n  row { submit \"Send\" }\n}"
      form{>https://formspree.io/f/your-id post g14
        in{n:name "Your name" req}
        in{n:email "E-mail" k:email ph"you@example.com" req}
        sel{n:topic "Topic" opt"Question" opt"Feedback"}
        area{n:message "Message" rows4}
        check{n:newsletter "Send me news"}
        r{send"Send"}
      }
    }
  }
  section{$id"sending" $title"Where the data goes"
    "`to` is the address that receives the form, and `method` is `get` (the default, for searches) or `post` (for messages). A static website can't store messages itself, so use a form service such as Formspree, Basin or Netlify Forms, or your own server."
    note{$title"Native viewer"
      "In the native SLML viewer forms are shown but can't be typed into yet. The optional web adapter (`slml serve --web --open`) and HTML exports support editing and submission. Native form interaction remains planned."
    }
  }
  section{$id"fields" $title"Fields"
    c{g0
      ref{$name"input" $values"kind, placeholder, value" $about"One line of text. kind is text, email, password, number, tel, url, date or search."}
      ref{$name"textarea" $values"rows, placeholder, value" $about"Several lines of text (rows: 1–50, default 4)."}
      ref{$name"checkbox" $values"checked" $about"A yes/no box. Its label is shown next to it."}
      ref{$name"select" $values"option …" $about"A drop-down list of options. option takes a label, an optional value and selected: true."}
      ref{$name"submit" $values"label" $about"The button that sends the form. Styled like button."}
    }
    "All fields need `name` (what the value is sent as) and `label` (what people see). `required: true` marks a field that must be filled in; its label gets a `*`."
    warning{$title"Rules"
      -{g4
        "Fields and submit only work inside a form, and forms can't be nested."
        "A field without a label is an error: screen readers and people both need it."
        "A select needs at least one option, and only one can be selected."
      }
    }
  }
  pager{$prev"/components.slml" $prev-label"Components and imports" $next"/sites.slml" $next-label"Building a website"}
}
